1	# Blocking Issues Fix Summary
2	
3	## Problem Analysis
4	
5	After implementing the hacking agents, tasks were blocking each other, preventing concurrent execution. The investigation revealed several root causes:
6	
7	### Root Causes Identified:
8	
9	1. **DNS Resolution Timeouts (PRIMARY ISSUE)**
10	   - `socket.gethostbyname()` and `socket.gethostbyaddr()` calls without timeouts
11	   - DNS resolution can hang for several minutes with slow/unresponsive DNS
12	   - Multiple locations in code performing DNS lookups without timeout handling
13	   - Tasks appearing to "hang" when actually waiting for DNS resolution
14	
15	2. **MongoDB Connection Bottleneck**
16	   - Single global MongoDB client without proper connection pooling
17	   - Limited connection timeout settings
18	   - No connection health management
19	
20	3. **MCP Resource Contention**
21	   - Each hacking agent creating its own MCP connection
22	   - No proper cleanup of MCP resources
23	   - Resource leaks causing connection exhaustion
24	
25	4. **Long-Running Operations Without Timeouts**
26	   - Hacking agent operations could run indefinitely
27	   - No timeout handling in task execution
28	   - Tasks hanging without proper error handling
29	
30	5. **Inadequate Resource Management**
31	   - Missing cleanup methods in hacking agent
32	   - No proper resource isolation between tasks
33	   - Shared resources causing blocking
34	
35	## Fixes Implemented
36	
37	### 1. DNS Resolution Timeout Fixes (PRIMARY FIX)
38	
39	**Files:** `src/red_team_mcp/fastmcp_server.py`, `src/red_team_mcp/database.py`, `src/red_team_mcp/nuclei_scanner.py`
40	
41	**Changes:**
42	- Added `asyncio.wait_for()` with 10-second timeout for FastMCP hostname resolution
43	- Implemented signal-based timeouts (3-5 seconds) for database hostname resolution
44	- Added timeout handling for nuclei scanner DNS resolution
45	- Added timeout handling for socket connection tests
46	
47	**Benefits:**
48	- Tasks no longer hang indefinitely waiting for DNS resolution
49	- Fast failure for unreachable/non-existent hostnames
50	- Improved user experience with predictable response times
51	
52	### 2. MongoDB Connection Pool Optimization
53	
54	**File:** `src/red_team_mcp/database.py`
55	
56	**Changes:**
57	- Increased connection pool size from default to 50 connections
58	- Added minimum pool size (5 connections)
59	- Configured proper timeouts:
60	  - `connectTimeoutMS=10000` (10 seconds)
61	  - `socketTimeoutMS=30000` (30 seconds)
62	  - `waitQueueTimeoutMS=5000` (5 seconds for pool wait)
63	- Added connection health checks with retry logic
64	- Implemented proper connection cleanup function
65	
66	**Benefits:**
67	- Multiple tasks can access database concurrently
68	- Better handling of connection failures
69	- Automatic connection recovery
70	
71	### 2. Hacking Agent Resource Management
72	
73	**File:** `src/agents/hacking_agent.py`
74	
75	**Changes:**
76	- Added proper `cleanup()` method to release MCP resources
77	- Implemented timeout handling for agent operations
78	- Added error handling for initialization failures
79	- Ensured MCP tools are properly closed after use
80	
81	**Benefits:**
82	- Prevents resource leaks
83	- Allows multiple hacking agents to run concurrently
84	- Better error recovery
85	
86	### 3. Task Execution Timeout Handling
87	
88	**File:** `src/agents/simple_agent.py`
89	
90	**Changes:**
91	- Added `asyncio.wait_for()` with configurable timeout
92	- Proper timeout exception handling
93	- Task status updates for timeout scenarios
94	- Better error reporting for failed tasks
95	
96	**Benefits:**
97	- Prevents tasks from hanging indefinitely
98	- Better user feedback on task status
99	- Improved system stability
100	
101	### 4. Resource Isolation Improvements
102	
103	**Multiple Files**
104	
105	**Changes:**
106	- Each task now has isolated resource access
107	- Proper cleanup in finally blocks
108	- Better exception handling to prevent resource locks
109	- Improved error propagation
110	
111	## Testing
112	
113	### Test Scripts
114	
115	#### 1. `test_dns_timeout_fix.py` (PRIMARY TEST)
116	
117	Tests DNS resolution timeout fixes:
118	
119	1. **FastMCP DNS Resolution**
120	   - Tests normal hostname resolution (google.com)
121	   - Tests timeout with non-existent domains
122	   - Verifies completion within 10-15 seconds
123	
124	2. **Database DNS Resolution**
125	   - Tests hostname resolution during scan result saving
126	   - Verifies timeout handling for invalid IPs
127	   - Checks completion within timeout limits
128	
129	3. **Nuclei Scanner DNS Resolution**
130	   - Tests DNS resolution in vulnerability scanning
131	   - Verifies timeout for non-existent hosts
132	   - Ensures fast failure instead of hanging
133	
134	4. **Basic Socket DNS Resolution**
135	   - Tests system-level DNS resolution behavior
136	   - Baseline for comparison with our fixes
137	
138	#### 2. `test_blocking_fix.py`
139	
140	Tests overall system behavior:
141	
142	1. **Concurrent Task Execution**
143	   - Starts multiple tasks simultaneously
144	   - Monitors task progress
145	   - Verifies tasks complete without blocking each other
146	
147	2. **Database Connection Management**
148	   - Tests multiple concurrent database operations
149	   - Verifies connection pool functionality
150	   - Checks for connection leaks
151	
152	### Expected Results
153	
154	After applying these fixes:
155	
156	- ✅ DNS resolution completes within 3-10 seconds (no more hanging)
157	- ✅ Tasks start executing immediately instead of appearing stuck
158	- ✅ Multiple tasks can run concurrently without DNS blocking
159	- ✅ Database operations don't block each other
160	- ✅ Hacking agents can run in parallel
161	- ✅ Tasks have proper timeout handling
162	- ✅ Resources are properly cleaned up
163	- ✅ Fast failure for unreachable hosts instead of indefinite waiting
164	
165	## Usage Recommendations
166	
167	### For Users:
168	
169	1. **Monitor Task Status**
170	   ```bash
171	   # Check running tasks
172	   tasks
173	   
174	   # View specific task details
175	   task <task-name>
176	   
177	   # Cancel stuck tasks if needed
178	   task <task-name> cancel
179	   ```
180	
181	2. **Use Appropriate Timeouts**
182	   - Default timeout is 300 seconds (5 minutes)
183	   - Increase for long-running operations: `--timeout 600`
184	   - Monitor task progress with `tasks` command
185	
186	3. **Resource Management**
187	   - Exit cleanly with `exit` command to cleanup resources
188	   - Don't force-kill the agent to avoid resource leaks
189	
