1	[![Verified on MseeP](https://mseep.ai/badge.svg)](https://mseep.ai/app/f159a924-db1c-42f8-825b-b8a1795c1437)
2	
3	# Kafka MCP Server
4	
5	A Message Context Protocol (MCP) server that integrates with Apache Kafka to provide publish and consume functionalities for LLM and Agentic applications.
6	
7	## Overview
8	
9	This project implements a server that allows AI models to interact with Kafka topics through a standardized interface. It supports:
10	
11	- Publishing messages to Kafka topics
12	- Consuming messages from Kafka topics
13	
14	## Prerequisites
15	
16	- Python 3.8+
17	- Apache Kafka instance
18	- Python dependencies (see Installation section)
19	
20	## Installation
21	
22	1. Clone the repository:
23	   ```bash
24	   git clone <repository-url>
25	   cd <repository-directory>
26	   ```
27	
28	2. Create a virtual environment and activate it:
29	   ```bash
30	   python -m venv venv
31	   source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows, use: venv\Scripts\activate
32	   ```
33	
34	3. Install the required dependencies:
35	   ```bash
36	   pip install -r requirements.txt
37	   ```
38	
39	   If no requirements.txt exists, install the following packages:
40	   ```bash
41	   pip install aiokafka python-dotenv pydantic-settings mcp-server
42	   ```
43	
44	## Configuration
45	
46	Create a `.env` file in the project root with the following variables:
47	
48	```
49	# Kafka Configuration
50	KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9092
51	TOPIC_NAME=your-topic-name
52	IS_TOPIC_READ_FROM_BEGINNING=False
53	DEFAULT_GROUP_ID_FOR_CONSUMER=kafka-mcp-group
54	
55	# Optional: Custom Tool Descriptions
56	# TOOL_PUBLISH_DESCRIPTION="Custom description for the publish tool"
57	# TOOL_CONSUME_DESCRIPTION="Custom description for the consume tool"
58	```
59	
60	## Usage
61	
62	### Running the Server
63	
64	You can run the server using the provided `main.py` script:
65	
66	```bash
67	python main.py --transport stdio
68	```
69	
70	Available transport options:
71	- `stdio`: Standard input/output (default)
72	- `sse`: Server-Sent Events
73	
74	### Integrating with Claude Desktop
75	
76	To use this Kafka MCP server with Claude Desktop, add the following configuration to your Claude Desktop configuration file:
77	
78	```json
79	{
80	    "mcpServers": {
81	        "kafka": {
82	            "command": "python",
83	            "args": [
84	                "<PATH TO PROJECTS>/main.py"
85	            ]
86	        }
87	    }
88	}
89	```
90	
91	Replace `<PATH TO PROJECTS>` with the absolute path to your project directory.
92	
93	## Project Structure
94	
95	- `main.py`: Entry point for the application
96	- `kafka.py`: Kafka connector implementation
97	- `server.py`: MCP server implementation with tools for Kafka interaction
98	- `settings.py`: Configuration management using Pydantic
99	
100	## Available Tools
101	
102	### kafka-publish
103	
104	Publishes information to the configured Kafka topic.
105	
106	### kafka-consume
107	
108	consume information from the configured Kafka topic.
109	- Note: once a message is read from the topic it can not be read again using the same groupid
110	
111	### Create-Topic
112	Creates a new Kafka topic with specified parameters.
113	- **Options**:
114	   - `--topic`Name of the topic to create
115	   - `--partitions`Number of partitions to allocate
116	   - `--replication-factor`Replication factor across brokers
117	   - `--config`(optional) Topic-level configuration overrides (e.g., `retention.ms=604800000`)
118	
119	### Delete-Topic
120	Deletes an existing Kafka topic.
121	- **Options**:
122	   - `--topic`Name of the topic to delete
123	   - `--timeout`(optional) Time to wait for deletion to complete
124	
125	### List-Topics
126	Lists all topics in the cluster (or filtered by pattern).
127	- **Options**:
128	   - `--bootstrap-server`Broker address
129	   - `--pattern`(optional) Regular expression to filter topic names
130	   - `--exclude-internal`(optional) Exclude internal topics (default: true)
131	
132	### Topic-Configuration
133	Displays or alters configuration for one or more topics.
134	- **Options**:
135	   - `--describe`Show current configs for a topic
136	   - `--alter`Modify configs (e.g., `--add-config retention.ms=86400000,--delete-config cleanup.policy`)
137	   - `--topic`Name of the topic
138	
139	### Topic-Metadata
140	Retrieves metadata about a topic or the cluster.
141	- **Options**:
142	   - `--topic`(If provided) Fetch metadata only for this topic
143	   - `--bootstrap-server`Broker address
144	   - `--include-offline`(optional) Include brokers or partitions that are offline  
145	

