[USER]:
1	# unreal-mcp-server
2	
3	unreal-mcp-server is a Python-based server that implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP) for Unreal Engine. 
4	It enables smooth communication between MCP clients (e.g., Claude, Cursor, Windsurf) and the Unreal Editor, and is intended to be used together with the Unreal-MCPython Plugin.
5	
6	- Demo : [Build 3D Scenes in Unreal Engine with Claude AI | Unreal-MCPython Demo](https://youtu.be/V7KyjzFlBLk?si=sOY1dEVGV2hqi4JC)
7	- Fab Link : [Unreal-MCPython: AI Assistant Plugin for Unreal Editor using Python & MCP](https://fab.com/s/aed5f75d50b2)
8	- Github Link : [GenOrca/unreal-mcpython](https://github.com/GenOrca/unreal-mcpython)
9	
10	
11	## 🎯 Why Choose Unreal-MCPython?
12	
13	<p align="center">
14	<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GenOrca/Screenshot/refs/heads/main/unreal-mcp/Screenshot%202025-06-02%20025106.png" width="400">
15	<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GenOrca/Screenshot/refs/heads/main/unreal-mcp/Screenshot%202025-06-02%20025111.png" width="400">
16	<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GenOrca/Screenshot/refs/heads/main/unreal-mcp/Screenshot%202025-06-02%20025115.png" width="400">
17	<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GenOrca/Screenshot/refs/heads/main/unreal-mcp/Screenshot%202025-06-02%20025120.png" width="400">
18	</p>
19	
20	- 🧠 **Unreal AI integration** - Direct Claude AI assistance in Unreal Engine
21	- 🔗 **Native MCP protocol support** - Seamless communication between AI and UE
22	- 🎮 **Intelligent game development** - AI-powered asset management and scene manipulation  
23	- ⚡ **Smart automation** - Context-aware blueprint scripting with AI guidance
24	- 🎨 **Technical artist focused** - AI assistance for complex production pipelines
25	
26	## Key Features
27	
28	- MCP server for communication with Unreal Engine
29	- Built-in routers for various operations (e.g., Actor, Asset, Editor, etc)
30	- Supports Python 3.11 and later
31	
32	# Installation
33	
34	Clone the repository:
35	
36	```bash
37	git clone https://github.com/your-org/unreal-mcp-server.git
38	cd unreal-mcp-server
39	```
40	
41	# Running the Server
42	
43	You can start the MCP server with the following command:
44	```bash
45	uv --directory absolute/path/to/unreal-mcp-server run src/unreal_mcp/main.py
46	```
47	
48	# Example Configuration (Using Claude, VSCode, Cursor)
49	
50	The following is an example configuration for launching the MCP server from Claude, VSCode, or Cursor:
51	
52	```json
53	{
54	    "mcpServers": {
55	        "unreal-mcpython": {
56	            "command": "uv",
57	            "args": [
58	                "--directory",
59	                "/absolute/path/to/unreal-mcp-server",  // e.g., D:/GitHub/unreal-mcp-server
60	                "run",
61	                "src/unreal_mcp/main.py"
62	            ]
63	        }
64	    }
65	}
66	```
67	
68	This configuration approach works similarly across editors like VSCode and Cursor.
69	
