237	        {
238	            "role": "user",
239	            "content": {
240	                "type": "text",
241	                "text": """
242	Please help me sort my inbox to achieve inbox zero by following these steps:
243	
244	0. First, get ready for the requests mail and calendar actions:
245	   - List email folders so you can see the email hierarchy
246	   - Get folder id dict: So can match folder names to folder ids
247	
248	1. Next, identify calendar invites and messages with scheduling requests:
249	   - For calendar invites: Check my calendar for conflicts, then either accept, draft a response, or draft counter-proposals
250	   - Looking for meeting requests without formal invites: If a mail header is from an individual and the subject looks conversational instead of like marketing, get the full email content to check it for meeting requests
251	   - If you checked a message content and it did not have a meeting request, file it in the relevant folder as per normal rules below
252	   - For meeting requests without formal invites: Check my calendar and draft calendar invites with appropriate details
253	
254	2. Next, identify important emails for filing in the Important folder:
255	   - Look for emails from key contacts (threads I've responded to, clients, team members)
256	   - Identify emails with urgent subject lines or time-sensitive content or suggesting an action
257	   - Move these to my "Important" folder using move_email_to_folder
258	
259	3. For all remaining emails:
